WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.025
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:08.607
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.907 --> 00:00:15.333
Unit six: Urban vs Rural Life. Today you will compare places with comparatives and superlatives.

4
00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:18.122
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:22.555
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:24.662
Metropolis.

7
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.555
Metropolis means a very large, busy city.

8
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.382
Bangkok is a huge metropolis.

9
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:34.601
Your turn. Say: Metropolis.

10
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:38.595
Metropolis.

11
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.421
Countryside.

12
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:44.798
Countryside means land outside towns with farms and nature.

13
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:47.708
My grandparents live in the countryside.

14
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:50.911
Your turn. Say: Countryside.

15
00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:54.872
Countryside.

16
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.210
Population density.

17
00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:01.958
Population density means how many people live in an area.

18
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.316
Phnom Penh has a high population density.

19
00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:09.138
Your turn. Say: Population density.

20
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.616
Population density.

21
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.734
Infrastructure.

22
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.642
Infrastructure means roads, bridges, power and water systems.

23
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.772
Good infrastructure helps business grow.

24
00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:27.291
Your turn. Say: Infrastructure.

25
00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.587
Infrastructure.

26
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.537
Agricultural.

27
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.840
Agricultural means related to farming.

28
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.914
Battambang is an agricultural province.

29
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:43.471
Your turn. Say: Agricultural.

30
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:47.741
Agricultural.

31
00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:49.682
Fast-paced.

32
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:53.472
Fast-paced means moving or happening quickly.

33
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:56.036
City life is fast-paced.

34
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.616
Your turn. Say: Fast-paced.

35
00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:03.723
Fast-paced.

36
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:05.403
Tranquil.

37
00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:08.416
Tranquil means calm and quiet.

38
00:02:09.017 --> 00:02:11.283
The village is tranquil at sunset.

39
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:14.408
Your turn. Say: Tranquil.

40
00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.186
Tranquil.

41
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.789
Commute.

42
00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:23.050
Commute means the trip to work or school.

43
00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.615
My commute takes forty minutes.

44
00:02:26.217 --> 00:02:28.579
Your turn. Say: Commute.

45
00:02:31.433 --> 00:02:32.388
Commute.

46
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.372
Community feel.

47
00:02:35.383 --> 00:02:38.521
Community feel means a sense of belonging with neighbours.

48
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:41.534
Villages have a strong community feel.

49
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.942
Your turn. Say: Community feel.

50
00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.080
Community feel.

51
00:02:49.817 --> 00:02:51.038
Urban sprawl.

52
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.373
Urban sprawl means a city spreading out into the countryside.

53
00:02:55.983 --> 00:02:58.993
Urban sprawl replaces rice fields with houses.

54
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:02.549
Your turn. Say: Urban sprawl.

55
00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.051
Urban sprawl.

56
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:09.247
Amenities.

57
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:14.072
Amenities means useful places like shops, hospitals and parks.

58
00:03:14.683 --> 00:03:16.590
The city has more amenities.

59
00:03:17.183 --> 00:03:19.662
Your turn. Say: Amenities.

60
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.524
Amenities.

61
00:03:24.283 --> 00:03:25.389
Lifestyle.

62
00:03:26.383 --> 00:03:28.812
Lifestyle means the way a person lives.

63
00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:31.242
I prefer a slower lifestyle.

64
00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.642
Your turn. Say: Lifestyle.

65
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.780
Lifestyle.

66
00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:43.450
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:44.283 --> 00:03:47.293
Visal, would you rather live in a city or the countryside?

68
00:03:48.383 --> 00:03:52.995
The city is busier and has more amenities, so I prefer it for now.

69
00:03:54.083 --> 00:03:55.677
But isn't your commute longer?

70
00:03:56.783 --> 00:04:03.058
Yes, the traffic is worse. My grandparents' village is the most peaceful place I know.

71
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.463
Which has the strongest community feel?

72
00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:13.082
The countryside. Everyone knows everyone, and life is more tranquil.

73
00:04:14.233 --> 00:04:15.629
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:16.483 --> 00:04:20.015
Grammar focus: Comparatives and superlatives.

75
00:04:20.315 --> 00:04:21.572
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:22.283 --> 00:04:24.248
The city is busier than the village.

77
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:27.672
The countryside is the most peaceful place.

78
00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:32.130
Traffic is worse in the city. It is the worst at five o'clock.

79
00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:40.635
Short adjectives take -er and -est. Long adjectives take 'more' and 'the most'. Good, better, best. Bad, worse, worst.

80
00:04:41.383 --> 00:04:45.673
Be careful! Don't say: The city is more busy than the village.

81
00:04:47.633 --> 00:04:50.678
Say: The city is busier than the village.

82
00:04:50.978 --> 00:04:52.548
Short adjectives take -er.

83
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:56.229
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.348
Two Ways to Live.

85
00:04:58.648 --> 00:05:03.190
City life in a metropolis is fast-paced, unlike the tranquil countryside.

86
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.850
The city is busier and has better infrastructure.

87
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:11.412
Urban areas offer more amenities, but the commute is longer.

88
00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.945
Rural life has a stronger community feel.

89
00:05:15.933 --> 00:05:19.988
For many people, the countryside is the most peaceful place to live.

90
00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:24.904
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.726
The city is blank than the village.

92
00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:31.935
A, busier. B, busiest. C, more busy.

93
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.209
The answer is A: busier.

94
00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:39.920
Calm and quiet is blank.

95
00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:44.489
A, tranquil. B, fast-paced. C, urban.

96
00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:49.859
The answer is A: tranquil.

97
00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.550
Roads, bridges and power systems are blank.

98
00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.817
A, infrastructure. B, amenities. C, sprawl.

99
00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:04.051
The answer is A: infrastructure.

100
00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:08.279
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:09.117 --> 00:06:12.547
Would you rather live in a city or the countryside? Why?

102
00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:22.839
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:30.667
I would rather live in the countryside. It is quieter and cleaner than the city, and the people are the friendliest I know.

104
00:06:30.967 --> 00:06:33.002
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:33.917 --> 00:06:38.798
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and comparatives and superlatives.

106
00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:42.865
Today's value is community. Help the people in your town.

107
00:06:43.165 --> 00:06:45.655
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:45.955 --> 00:06:49.304
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

